From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: raise the Pocket ACE speaker digital cap to 0 dB

The machine driver limits the WSA digital volume to -3 dB and the PA
volume to 0 dB on every board, "until we have active speaker
protection". On the Pocket ACE that leaves the speakers too quiet with
the slider at the top: both controls sit at their limits, and the amps
run at 0 dB fixed gain (DRE_CTL_1 0x1d: CSR_GAIN_EN set, gain code 14).

Let the ACE reach 84, which is 0 dB. That is unity, so it cannot clip
the signal, and it is the control's register default, so no UCM change
is needed. The PA limit stays at 0 dB and every other board keeps -3 dB.

The speakers see +3 dB, twice the power at peaks, and still have no
active protection.

Signed-off-by: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index 4bebc51..f62a999 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -179,6 +179,7 @@ static int sc8280xp_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 	struct snd_soc_dai *cpu_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_cpu(rtd, 0);
 	struct snd_soc_card *card = rtd->card;
 	struct snd_soc_jack *dp_jack  = NULL;
+	int wsa_digital_max = 81;
 	int dp_pcm_id = 0;
 
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
@@ -188,9 +189,15 @@ static int sc8280xp_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 		 * Set limit of -3 dB on Digital Volume and 0 dB on PA Volume
 		 * to reduce the risk of speaker damage until we have active
 		 * speaker protection in place.
+		 *
+		 * The Pocket ACE speakers are too quiet at that limit, so
+		 * allow 0 dB of Digital Volume (unity) there.
 		 */
-		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA_RX0 Digital Volume", 81);
-		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA_RX1 Digital Volume", 81);
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("ayaneo,pocketace"))
+			wsa_digital_max = 84;
+
+		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA_RX0 Digital Volume", wsa_digital_max);
+		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA_RX1 Digital Volume", wsa_digital_max);
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "SpkrLeft PA Volume", 17);
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "SpkrRight PA Volume", 17);
 		break;
